  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between SGI-1776 and SMMC-7721 through a series of target interactions. SGI-1776 is implicated in targeting Solute carrier family 12 member 5, which is a target of both Fumiquinazoline B and Arillanin A. These compounds, in turn, have targets that ultimately lead to SMMC-7721. This indicates that SGI-1776 may act through a shared pathway involving members of the solute carrier family, which are involved in transport processes critical for cellular function. The presence of multiple targets that ultimately point to SMMC-7721 suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the modulation of transport proteins, potentially affecting cellular processes that are essential for the survival or function of the SMMC-7721 cell line. The evidence supports a role for SGI-1776 in modulating these transport proteins, which may contribute to its effect on SMMC-7721.",
